{:id :EACL-FORMAL-019
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :production-source-refinement-review
 :seed-or-trace
 "ordered-merge/descending/maximum-eid-as-first-value"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :authorization-result
 :affected-versions
 ["PR 101 worktree before explicit ordered-merge last-value presence"]
 :affected-backends [:shared :datomic :datascript :datahike]
 :root-cause
 "The optimized descending host merge used the runtime's maximum integer as the sentinel for ‘no previously emitted value’. When that maximum was a legitimate first EID, duplicate suppression mistook it for an already emitted value and dropped it. The Dafny merge carries explicit state and did not contain the defect."
 :fix
 "Ascending and descending specialized merges now carry an explicit `has-last?` bit independently of the last EID. Every integer value, including the runtime maximum, is therefore distinct from the uninitialized state."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.backend.v8-test/descending-merge-retains-maximum-eid-test"
  "formal/dafny/OrderedMerge.dfy source-specialization oracle"
  "formal mutation :ordered-merge-wrong-comparator"]}
